     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've flagged the run as anomalous, with a blocked exhaust as the likely cause. Tube pressure climbed steadily during growth, from about 3.05 to 3.49 Torr (t = 2640–3240 s). It had held near 3.04 Torr until then, and nothing changed in the setpoints. Argon flow stayed at 100 sccm, so extra gas coming in doesn't explain it. Exhaust oxygen stayed at 4–6 ppm, which argues against air leaking in through a seal. Temperature is holding at 750 °C with steady heater power.\n\nThe next step I'd suggest is to check the exhaust side directly: pump inlet pressure, exhaust valve position, and whether a trap or filter is clogging. This data had no normal-run pressure reference, so I can't say exactly how far outside normal the rise is. There's no characterisation of the sample yet, and because of this fault, any result from this run may not tell us much about the recipe."
     }
